---
import GuideLayout from '../../layouts/GuideLayout.astro';
import IntermediateNav from '../../components/IntermediateNav.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<GuideLayout title="Intermediate Efficiency · RuneScape Adventure Guide" current="intermediate">
  <div class="page-grid intermediate-overview-grid">
    <aside class="sidebar"><IntermediateNav current="overview" /></aside>
    <article class="content">
      <header class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-kicker">Intermediate Efficiency</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">Build your Ironman with a clear, relaxed route.</h1>
        <p class="chapter-summary">For players who know RuneScape and want help with what comes next. This guide adapts BRUHsailer's quest and unlock order, explains where to get supplies, and gives you a reason and a stopping point for each grind. Follow it one quest at a time, with low-attention training options along the way.</p>
      </header>

      <section>
        <div class="section-label">How this guide works</div>
        <h2>Use this guide by itself.</h2>
        <div class="principle-grid">
          <div class="principle"><strong>Complete route.</strong><span>You do not need BRUHsailer open in another tab. Required quests, items, quantities, training targets and important future pickups are written into this route.</span></div>
          <div class="principle"><strong>Unlock useful things early.</strong><span>Build travel options, start Farming Contracts, unlock Ancient Magicks and establish ways to earn money as the quests begin to need them.</span></div>
          <div class="principle"><strong>Take one quest at a time.</strong><span>Finish each quest before moving on, unless the step gives you a reason to pause it—for example, to wait for a timer or unlock fairy rings early.</span></div>
          <div class="principle"><strong>Default to chill skilling.</strong><span>AFK and low-attention methods are recommended first. Faster methods remain visible, but blackjacking, 2-tick methods and other high-input techniques are never assumed.</span></div>
          <div class="principle"><strong>Do diaries for useful rewards.</strong><span>Complete diaries when their rewards help with the next part of the guide. Small tasks can wait unless you are already passing them.</span></div>
          <div class="principle"><strong>Know what to keep.</strong><span>When you need an item later, the step tells you how many to bank and which quest or activity will use them.</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="callout"><strong>Using Quest Helper:</strong> use it for dialogue choices, puzzle solutions and object locations during a quest. Read the preparation here before setting out so you have the items, levels and travel options you need.</div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <div class="section-label">Chapter 1</div>
        <h2>Get to da chopper earth staves — intermediate edition.</h2>
        <p>Start at Tutorial Island, gather Wintertodt supplies, train Fishing, Agility and Thieving, then unlock Fossil Island birdhouse runs, fairy rings and protection prayers. Start regular Farming runs and easy contracts when you can, complete Desert Treasure, and bank Earth orbs to turn into battlestaves for money in Chapter 2.</p>
        <div class="callout"><strong>By the end of Chapter 1:</strong> expect roughly 46 Attack · 50 Strength · 34 Defence · 39 Hitpoints · 45 Ranged · 43 Prayer · 63 Magic · 24 Runecraft · 39 Construction · 50+ Agility · 40 Herblore · at least 53 Thieving for Desert Treasure · 58 Crafting, or at least 54 with enough banked mushroom pies · roughly 47–48 Fletching (train to 46 when asked) · 20+ Slayer · 46 Hunter · 44 Mining · 42 Smithing · 65+ Fishing · 60 Cooking · 89 Firemaking · 70 Woodcutting. Agility and Fishing targets are unboosted levels. You will also have full Rogue and will have saved at least 1.35m coins in 1.2, with some of that money spent on later supplies. <strong>Your Farming level will depend on the seeds you obtained and the runs you completed;</strong> check for 49 at Fairytale II and train to an unboosted 70 before Song of the Elves. Fishing may be higher if you used more Barbarian Fishing to train Agility. Use the individual steps for each requirement; extra quests and your choice of training methods can change the levels you finish with.</div>
        <div class="chapter-card-grid">
          <a class="subchapter-card" href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-1/`}><span>1.1</span><strong>Wintertodt foundation</strong><small>Tutorial Island → early quests and Ardougne cloak 1 → four warm items → 50 Firemaking → Wintertodt.</small></a>
          <a class="subchapter-card" href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-2/`}><span>1.2</span><strong>Fishing & Thieving</strong><small>Desert quests, optional Angler, Waterfall, Barbarian Fishing, movement stats and the cash reserve.</small></a>
          <a class="subchapter-card" href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-3/`}><span>1.3</span><strong>Bird runs & infrastructure</strong><small>Bones to Peaches, Fossil Island, birdhouses, teleport jewelry, fairy rings and the Farming quest chain.</small></a>
          <a class="subchapter-card" href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/`}><span>1.4</span><strong>Farming, Desert Treasure & earth orbs</strong><small>70 Woodcutting, 43 Prayer, regular Farming runs, Desert Treasure and Earth orbs for battlestaves.</small></a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <div class="section-label">Chapter 2</div>
        <h2>Turn the foundation into a quest-ready account.</h2>
        <p>Turn your banked Earth orbs into money for Construction and house travel, complete quests to reach new areas, and learn Sailing. Set up your kingdom, unlock Lunar spells and Barrows gloves, then work toward a dragon defender, Piety and the Morytania quests. Complete useful quests before training the remaining skills for Song of the Elves, which unlocks Prifddinas at the end of the chapter.</p>
        <div class="chapter-card-grid">
          <a class="subchapter-card" href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-2-1/`}><span>2.1</span><strong>Cash & Construction Backbone</strong><small>Earth battlestaves → alchemy cash → Adept contracts and plank sack → mahogany eagle lectern → house tablets.</small></a>
          <a class="subchapter-card" href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-2-2/`}><span>2.2</span><strong>Quest Infrastructure</strong><small>Dragon Slayer I → Iban's staff → Shilo and Dorgesh-Kaan → Heroes' Quest → Monkey Madness I.</small></a>
          <a class="subchapter-card" href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-2-3/`}><span>2.3</span><strong>Sailing, Combat & the Kingdom</strong><small>Miscellania → 40 Slayer → Royal Trouble → Horror from the Deep → learn Sailing to level 45.</small></a>
          <a class="subchapter-card" href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-2-4/`}><span>2.4</span><strong>Lunar, Cooking & Recipe for Disaster</strong><small>Fremennik Isles → 60 Mining → Lunar → Swan Song → 70 Cooking → RFD and Barrows gloves.</small></a>
          <a class="subchapter-card" href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-2-5/`}><span>2.5</span><strong>Defender, Piety & Morytania</strong><small>Temple Knights → full Legends → dragon defender and Piety → Sins of the Father → Great Conch.</small></a>
          <a class="subchapter-card" href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-2-6/`}><span>2.6</span><strong>The 70s: Song of the Elves Preparation</strong><small>Useful quest XP → Sailing, Ranged and Hunter breaks → all eight unboosted level-70 requirements.</small></a>
          <a class="subchapter-card" href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-2-7/`}><span>2.7</span><strong>The Elf Finale · Prifddinas unlock</strong><small>Regicide → Roving Elves → Mourning's End I/II → Song of the Elves and Prifddinas.</small></a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <div class="section-label">Chapter 3</div>
        <h2>Chapter 3 — Quest Cape &amp; Fire Cape</h2>
        <p>Finish the remaining quests, earn a Fire Cape, and build the travel options, supplies and boss experience to choose your own direction afterward. <strong>The goal is a Quest Cape and Fire Cape.</strong> You can then pursue Bowfa and crystal armour, raids, Zulrah, Vorkath, Muspah, God Wars Dungeon, other gear upgrades, diaries, Combat Achievements, collection log goals, relaxed play or eventual 99s. Those later goals are optional, and you can finish this guide without an Enhanced Crystal Weapon Seed.</p>
        <div class="chapter-card-grid">
          <a class="subchapter-card" href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-3-1/`}><span>3.1</span><strong>Slayer Foundation &amp; While Guthix Sleeps</strong><small>Pirate quests → Slayer training → Path of Glouphrie → any remaining Magic training → WGS.</small></a>
          <a class="subchapter-card" href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-3-2/`}><span>3.2</span><strong>Varlamore, Wyrmscraig &amp; Runecraft</strong><small>Moons and Heart → staged Runecraft quests → Fallen From Grace → Final Dawn → Fremennik Exiles.</small></a>
          <a class="subchapter-card" href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-3-3/`}><span>3.3</span><strong>Ranged Foundation &amp; Fire Cape</strong><small>62 Ranged for Arrav → make a crossbow and ammunition → train Ranged in two stages → Jad and the Fire Cape.</small></a>
          <a class="subchapter-card" href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-3-4/`}><span>3.4</span><strong>Slayer Backbone, Monkey Madness II &amp; Theatre</strong><small>Check your cash → train Crafting and Slayer for MM2 → train Magic on Slayer tasks → Entry Mode and unboosted 75 Magic.</small></a>
          <a class="subchapter-card" href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-3-5/`}><span>3.5</span><strong>Quest Cleanup, Dragon Slayer II &amp; Desert Treasure II</strong><small>Quest cleanup → DS2 → Runecraft 60 → DT2 and the final pre-Drakan combat progression.</small></a>
          <a class="subchapter-card" href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-3-6/`}><span>3.6</span><strong>Blood Moon Rises &amp; Graduation</strong><small>Train the final four required skills → Vampyrium → Lowerniel Drakan → Quest Cape → choose your own endgame.</small></a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="source-note">
        <div class="section-label">Source & attribution</div>
        <p>This guide adapts the quest and account progression developed by So Iron BRUH and ParasailerOSRS in <a href="https://umkyzn.github.io/BRUHsailer/" rel="noreferrer">BRUHsailer</a>, with more explanations and a preference for relaxed training. Visit the original if you want to compare training and travel methods; everything you need to follow this route is included here.</p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>
</GuideLayout>
